t":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-10-22T14:03:56Z","updated_at":"2025-10-22T20:48:03Z","closed_at":"2025-10-22T20:47:57Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce MX110 (NVIDIA; 31.0.15.4629) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-8265U CPU @ 1.60GHz (8 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn GDScript editor, when using an **is** type check to verify the type of an InputEvent (or any other base type), the IDE does not narrow the type for autocomplete or warnings. For example:\n\n```GDscript\nfunc movePlayer(event: InputEvent) -> void:\n    if event.is_pressed() and event is InputEventKey:\n        # Even after trying to assert the type, the IDE still treats `event` as InputEvent\n        var key_event: InputEventKey = event\n        key_event.keycode\n```\nEven though the runtime type is correctly InputEventKey, the editor continues to treat event as the base InputEvent, requiring a separate typed variable to access type-specific members.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nNo need to reproduce just try copypaste and test the autocompletion.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNo need to reproduce just try copypaste and test the autocompletion.","closed_by":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDA